message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The Interface Between Safety Assurance and Formal Verification in NASA Gateway Autonomous Systems: A Traceability Gap in Public Documentation"
version: "1.0.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24559255"
date-released: "2026-11-26"
license: CC-BY-4.0
type: generic
url: "https://nasa-gateway.netlify.app"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gitdeeper16/NASA-GATEWAY"
abstract: >-
  A documentary analysis examining whether safety-derived boundaries of local
  autonomy can be traced to formally verifiable decision and escalation rules
  at the interface between Module System Managers (MSMs) and the Vehicle System
  Manager (VSM) in NASA Gateway. The reviewed public documentation does not
  establish a complete traceability chain from hazard-derived autonomy
  boundaries to specific MSM decision and escalation rules and their
  corresponding verification properties. The finding concerns public
  documentation only and makes no claim about implementation.
keywords:
  - NASA Gateway
  - autonomous systems
  - safety assurance
  - formal verification
  - Vehicle System Manager
  - Module System Manager
  - fault management
  - assume-guarantee contracts
  - runtime verification
  - control authority
  - traceability
